// Test: bugfixes/com001_capability_class_void_method_no_drop
// Grammar: capability_decl · class_decl.can_clause · dynamic dispatch on void method
// Semantic: COM001 (fingerprint 58bb119efe2e, surfaced 2026-07-19 while
//   verifying the primary COM001 fix via
//   tests/cln/core/capabilities/009_dynamic_dispatch.cln).
//
// Root cause: src/codegen/mir_codegen/instructions.rs::generate_call_capability
//   decides whether to emit a `Drop` after each dispatched Call based on
//   whether the callee "returns something". The check was
//     !matches!(f.return_type, MirType::Void)
//   which missed the legacy `MirType::Ptr(Box::new(MirType::Void))` encoding
//   that void class methods actually carry (see blocks.rs:288-289 for the
//   same pattern in the function-signature builder). Result: a spurious
//   Drop after a void `draw()` call in capability dispatch, which then
//   tripped wasmparser with "expected a type but nothing on stack" because
//   the Drop had no value to pop.
//
// This regression surfaced ONLY after the `has_capabilities` fix landed —
//   before that, capability class methods were static (no `this` param),
//   there was no dispatch to draw at all through CallCapability, and the
//   Drop path was never taken.
//
// Fix (0.33.109+): callee_returns_something now recognises both
//   MirType::Void AND MirType::Ptr(Void) as "no WASM return value".
//   Matches the void-detection pattern already in blocks.rs.
//
// This pin covers the void return case with multiple conforming classes
//   (2+ arms in the dispatch switch). If either the void detection or the
//   has_capabilities fix regresses, this test's output will fail (either
//   codegen error or wrong output).
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.109
//
// Expected output:
//   circle
//   square

start:
	Circle c = Circle()
	Square s = Square()
	render(c)
	render(s)

can Draw:
	draw()

class Circle can Draw
	functions:
		public:
			draw()
				print("circle")

class Square can Draw
	functions:
		public:
			draw()
				print("square")

functions:
	render(Draw shape)
		shape.draw()
